direction: right
threads: NuttX or Zephyr in this study {
  direction: down
  owners: 20 independent service threads {
    a: Thread A\n4 KiB stack
    b: Thread B\n4 KiB stack
    c: Other threads\n4 KiB each
  }
  scheduler: Preemptive OS scheduler\n10 ms timeslice {style.fill: "#eff6ff"}
  cpu: One 240 MHz core
  owners.a -> scheduler
  owners.b -> scheduler
  owners.c -> scheduler
  scheduler -> cpu
}
async: Embassy in this study {
  direction: down
  owners: 20 independent service tasks {
    a: Task A\nfuture state
    b: Task B\nfuture state
    c: Other tasks\nfuture state
  }
  executor: One cooperative executor\nawait Pending or hand off {style.fill: "#f0fdfa"}
  cpu: One core\n8 KiB shared stack
  owners.a -> executor
  owners.b -> executor
  owners.c -> executor
  executor -> cpu
}
note: "Conceptual services and queue capacities are unchanged.\nSeparate thread stacks and saved async state are different execution storage.\nThe single-executor model cannot preempt a synchronous CPU handler." {shape: text}
